{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "Please produce fluorescent ICAM-1-displaying virus-like particles (VLPs) and test their binding to our target cells by flow cytometry following the steps below. We will provide the plasmids (psPAX2 fluorescent core, pCMV6-ICAM-1, and negative control constructs) and the target cells.\n\n1. Seed HEK293T cells at 5 \u00d7 10^6 cells per 10 cm dish in 10 mL complete DMEM (DMEM with 10% heat-inactivated FBS and 10 mM HEPES) and incubate overnight at 37 \u00b0C, 5% CO2 to reach 70%\u201380% confluency.\n2. For each dish, prepare the transfection mix by combining 8 \u03bcg of psPAX2 fluorescent plasmid (mNeon preferred, or TagBFP/mScarlet) and 4 \u03bcg of ligand plasmid (pCMV6-ICAM-1 or control) in 500 \u03bcL Opti-MEM. In a separate tube, add 36 \u03bcL X-tremeGENE 9 to 500 \u03bcL Opti-MEM. Mix the two solutions together (1 mL total), incubate at room temperature for 15 minutes, and add dropwise to the cells.\n3. At 16\u201324 hours post-transfection, carefully replace the medium with 10 mL of fresh complete DMEM. \n4. At 48 hours post-transfection, collect the supernatant (~9 mL), pass it through a 0.45 \u03bcm syringe filter into a 15 mL conical tube, and mix with 3 mL Lenti-X Concentrator. Incubate overnight at 4 \u00b0C.\n5. Centrifuge the mixture at 1,500 \u00d7 g for 45 minutes at 4 \u00b0C. Aspirate all supernatant completely and resuspend the pellet thoroughly in 90 \u03bcL sterile PBS to create a 100\u00d7 stock. Aliquot and freeze at -80 \u00b0C (or proceed directly to assay).\n6. Harvest target cells (Jurkat, THP-1, or our test samples) at 350 \u00d7 g for 5 minutes and resuspend them directly in serum-free binding buffer (RPMI + GlutaMAX with 0.1% BSA) at 1\u20132 \u00d7 10^6 cells/mL. Seed 50 \u03bcL per well (5 \u00d7 10^4 to 1 \u00d7 10^5 cells) in a 96-well V-bottom plate.\n7. Add 50 \u03bcL of 2\u00d7 activation buffer (10 mM MgCl2, 4 mM EGTA in binding buffer; yielding 5 mM Mg2+ / 2 mM EGTA final) to each well.\n8. Immediately add 1\u20135 \u03bcL of the 100\u00d7 VLP stock per well (titrating between 1:100 and 1:20 final dilution), mix by pipetting, and incubate at 37 \u00b0C for 10 minutes.\n9. Fix immediately by adding 33 \u03bcL of cold 4% PFA directly to each well (1% final concentration), mix, and incubate on ice for 20 minutes.\n10. Pellet cells at 350 \u00d7 g for 3 minutes, discard supernatant, and wash twice with 250 \u03bcL FACS buffer (PBS with 0.2% BSA), spinning at 350 \u00d7 g for 3 minutes each time.\n11. Resuspend the washed cell pellets in 200 \u03bcL FACS buffer and acquire on the flow cytometer (acquiring ~140 \u03bcL per well). If necessary, fixed plates can be stored at 4 \u00b0C protected from light for up to 3 days before acquisition.\n\nPlease report the raw FCS files alongside gated singlet population histograms and median fluorescence intensities (MFI) for each sample and control condition.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 5781, "candidatesTokenCount": 867, "totalTokenCount": 8671, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 5781}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 2023, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.8-flash", "responseId": "kqP2asLaCKq5sOIPgNXUgQs"}